Z||000013||Cliff Pennock||12-03-2001||08:44 AM||||Although the technology driving it may be nice/awesome/spectacular, it's still nothing more than a contraption to move you from point A to B. That said, all this expensive technology does is simply replacing a third wheel (for balance) a throttle (for going forward), a brake (for braking) and a steering wheel (for steering).<P>So what's the big deal? What is all this "it's going to change the world" hype about? Are people to dumb to handle a throttle and a brake? Will the elimination of this suddenly prompt all people to buy such a thing? It's still impractical. It doesn't fit your suitcase. You'll get angry looks if you take this into an elevator. It takes up valuable space in your car.<P>I was expecting much more than this. Can anyone say "Sinclair"?<p>[This message has been edited by Cliff Pennock (edited 12-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||Oreif||12-03-2001||09:02 AM||||Just saw it demonstraited on TV. Looks like an expensive "toy". For it to become a "world<BR>changing device", It will require more practical uses. I can't see an entire city using this for transportation. <P>The only use I can see for it in it's present state would be in a large factory.<P>From a "hot rodder's" view,   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Can it be lowered? How wide a tire can go on it? How much horsepower can be added with a Flux capacitor? What is the 0-60 foot speed rating? What about security? Can it be equipped with Lo-Jac? The only options I can see would be tassles on the handle bars and saddle bags. (There was a guy on TV who had saddle bags and a stereo on his!)<P>The technology used may help with other things, Active handling on the Z07 Corvette that eliminates body roll of the car! HMM the possibilities are endless.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P><BR>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">            <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-03-2001).]||||reg||1
