Z||000031||Ken Wittlief||12-03-2001||05:36 PM||||I think the big deal about it is that it takes something we do instinctively and without conscience thought, walking, and extends it to 12 or 20mph at the upper end<P> and apparently it works on ice and snow as well.<P> If it will last for 20 years without wearing out and you live in the city or a small town, I can see this becoming popular with policemen and postmen, and people who do a lot of walking in their line of work<P> and then expanding out to short distance commuters - all the speed of a 10 speed bike, without the risks of falling down, and without the sweat<P> if it werent for the hype, and you had seen it this morning with no preconceptions, then I think we would all be saying, "WOW! Thats awesome - I want one!"||||reg||10
